NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001244 "First element ($status_code) is an integer containing HTTP-like status code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001245 "(200 means OK, 4xx caller error, 5xx function error). Second element"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001246 "($reason) is a string containing error message, or something like \"OK\" if status is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001247 "200. Third element ($payload) is the actual result, but usually not present when enveloped result is an error response ($status_code is not 2xx). Fourth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001248 "element (%result_meta) is called result metadata and is optional, a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001249 "that contains extra information, much like how HTTP response headers provide additional metadata."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001250 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001251 "Return value:  (any)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001252 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001253 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001254 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001255 "=head2 shortest_name"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001256 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001257 "Usage:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001258 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001259 " shortest_name(%args) -> [$status_code, $reason, $payload, \\%result_meta]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001260 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001261 "Return file(s) with the shortest name in one or more directories."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001262 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001263 "Notes:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001264 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001265 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001266 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001267 "=item * by default dotfiles are not included, use C<--all> (C<-a>) to include them"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001268 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001269 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001270 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001271 "Some examples:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001272 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001273 " # return file with the shortest name in current directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001274 " % shortest-name -f"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001275 " "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001276 " # return file(s) with the shortest name in /some/dir. if there are multiple"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001277 " # files with the same length, they will all be returned."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001278 " % shortest-name -N1 -f /some/dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001279 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001280 "This function is not exported by default, but exportable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001281 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001282 "Arguments ('*' denotes required arguments):"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001283 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001284 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001285 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001286 "=item * B<all> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001287 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001288 "Do not ignore entries starting with ."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001289 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001290 "=item * B<detail> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001291 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001292 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001293 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001294 "=item * B<dirs> => I<array[dirname]> (default: [\".\"])"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001295 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001296 "Directory to sort files of, defaults to current directory."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001297 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001298 "=item * B<exclude_filename_pattern> => I<re_from_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001299 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001300 "Exclude filenames that match a regex pattern."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001301 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001302 "=item * B<include_filename_pattern> => I<re_from_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001303 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001304 "Only include filenames that match a regex pattern."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001305 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001306 "=item * B<num_ranks> => I<uint>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001307 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001308 "Number of ranks to return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001309 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001310 "Difference between C<num_results> and C<num_ranks>: C<num_results> (C<-n> option)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001311 "specifies number of results regardless of ranks while C<num_ranks> (C<-N> option)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001312 "returns number of ranks. For example, if sorting is by reverse size and if"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001313 "C<num_results> is set to 1 and there are 2 files with the same largest size then"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001314 "only 1 of those files will be returned. With C<num_ranks> set to 1, both files"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001315 "will be returned because are they both rank #1."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001316 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001317 "=item * B<num_results> => I<uint>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001318 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001319 "Number of results to return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001320 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001321 "=item * B<recursive> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001322 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001323 "Recurse into subdirectories."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001324 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001325 "=item * B<type> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001326 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001327 "Only include files of certain type."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001328 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001329 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001330 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001331 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001332 "Returns an enveloped result (an array)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001333 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001334 "First element ($status_code) is an integer containing HTTP-like status code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001335 "(200 means OK, 4xx caller error, 5xx function error). Second element"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001336 "($reason) is a string containing error message, or something like \"OK\" if status is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001337 "200. Third element ($payload) is the actual result, but usually not present when enveloped result is an error response ($status_code is not 2xx). Fourth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001338 "element (%result_meta) is called result metadata and is optional, a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001339 "that contains extra information, much like how HTTP response headers provide additional metadata."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001340 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001341 "Return value:  (any)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001342 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001343 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001344 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001345 "=head2 smallest"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001346 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001347 "Usage:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001348 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001349 " smallest(%args) -> [$status_code, $reason, $payload, \\%result_meta]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001350 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001351 "Return the smallest file(s) in one or more directories."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001352 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001353 "Some examples:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001354 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001355 " # return smallest file in current directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001356 " % smallest -f"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001357 " "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001358 " # return smallest file(s) in /some/dir (if there are multiple files with the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001359 " # same size they will all be returned"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001360 " % smallest -N1 -f /some/dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001361 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001362 "This function is not exported by default, but exportable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001363 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001364 "Arguments ('*' denotes required arguments):"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001365 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001366 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001367 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001368 "=item * B<all> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001369 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001370 "Do not ignore entries starting with ."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001371 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001372 "=item * B<detail> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001373 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001374 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001375 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001376 "=item * B<dirs> => I<array[dirname]> (default: [\".\"])"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001377 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001378 "Directory to sort files of, defaults to current directory."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001379 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001380 "=item * B<exclude_filename_pattern> => I<re_from_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001381 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001382 "Exclude filenames that match a regex pattern."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001383 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001384 "=item * B<include_filename_pattern> => I<re_from_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001385 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001386 "Only include filenames that match a regex pattern."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001387 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001388 "=item * B<num_ranks> => I<uint>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001389 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001390 "Number of ranks to return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001391 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001392 "Difference between C<num_results> and C<num_ranks>: C<num_results> (C<-n> option)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001393 "specifies number of results regardless of ranks while C<num_ranks> (C<-N> option)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001394 "returns number of ranks. For example, if sorting is by reverse size and if"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001395 "C<num_results> is set to 1 and there are 2 files with the same largest size then"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001396 "only 1 of those files will be returned. With C<num_ranks> set to 1, both files"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001397 "will be returned because are they both rank #1."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001398 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001399 "=item * B<num_results> => I<uint>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001400 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001401 "Number of results to return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001402 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001403 "=item * B<recursive> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001404 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001405 "Recurse into subdirectories."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001406 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001407 "=item * B<type> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001408 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001409 "Only include files of certain type."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001410 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001411 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001412 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001413 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001414 "Returns an enveloped result (an array)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001415 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001416 "First element ($status_code) is an integer containing HTTP-like status code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001417 "(200 means OK, 4xx caller error, 5xx function error). Second element"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001418 "($reason) is a string containing error message, or something like \"OK\" if status is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001419 "200. Third element ($payload) is the actual result, but usually not present when enveloped result is an error response ($status_code is not 2xx). Fourth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001420 "element (%result_meta) is called result metadata and is optional, a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001421 "that contains extra information, much like how HTTP response headers provide additional metadata."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001422 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001423 "Return value:  (any)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001424 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001425 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001426 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001427 "=head2 sort_files"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001428 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001429 "Usage:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001430 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001431 " sort_files(%args) -> [$status_code, $reason, $payload, \\%result_meta]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001432 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001433 "Sort files in one or more directories and display the result in a flexible way."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001434 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001435 "This function is not exported by default, but exportable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001436 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001437 "Arguments ('*' denotes required arguments):"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001438 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001439 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001440 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001441 "=item * B<all> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001442 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001443 "Do not ignore entries starting with ."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001444 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001445 "=item * B<by_code> => I<code_from_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001446 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001447 "Perl code to sort."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001448 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001449 "=item * B<by_field> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001450 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001451 "Field name to sort against."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001452 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001453 "=item * B<by_sortsub> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001454 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001455 "Sort::Sub routine name to sort."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001456 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001457 "=item * B<detail> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001458 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001459 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001460 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001461 "=item * B<dirs> => I<array[dirname]> (default: [\".\"])"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001462 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001463 "Directory to sort files of, defaults to current directory."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001464 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001465 "=item * B<exclude_filename_pattern> => I<re_from_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001466 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001467 "Exclude filenames that match a regex pattern."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001468 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001469 "=item * B<include_filename_pattern> => I<re_from_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001470 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001471 "Only include filenames that match a regex pattern."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001472 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001473 "=item * B<key> => I<code_from_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001474 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001475 "Perl code to generate key to sort against."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001476 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001477 "If C<key> option is not specified, then: 1) if sorting is C<by_code> then the code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001478 "will receive files as records (hashes) with keys like C<name>, C<size>, etc; 2) if"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001479 "sorting is C<by_field> then the associated field is used as key; 3) if sorting is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001480 "C<by_sortsub> then by default the C<name> field will be used as the key."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001481 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001482 "To select a field, use this:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001483 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001484 " '$_->{FIELDNAME}'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001485 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001486 "for example:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001487 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001488 " '$_->{size}'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001489 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001490 "Another example, to generate length of name as key:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001491 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001492 " 'length($_->{name})'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001493 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001494 "=item * B<num_ranks> => I<uint>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001495 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001496 "Number of ranks to return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001497 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001498 "Difference between C<num_results> and C<num_ranks>: C<num_results> (C<-n> option)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001499 "specifies number of results regardless of ranks while C<num_ranks> (C<-N> option)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001500 "returns number of ranks. For example, if sorting is by reverse size and if"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001501 "C<num_results> is set to 1 and there are 2 files with the same largest size then"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001502 "only 1 of those files will be returned. With C<num_ranks> set to 1, both files"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001503 "will be returned because are they both rank #1."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001504 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001505 "=item * B<num_results> => I<uint>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001506 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001507 "Number of results to return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001508 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001509 "=item * B<recursive> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001510 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001511 "Recurse into subdirectories."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001512 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001513 "=item * B<reverse> => I<true>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001514 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001515 "Reverse order of sorting."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001516 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001517 "=item * B<sortsub_args> => I<hash>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001518 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001519 "Arguments to pass to Sort::Sub routine."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001520 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001521 "=item * B<type> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001522 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001523 "Only include files of certain type."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001524 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001525 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001526 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001527 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001528 "Returns an enveloped result (an array)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001529 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001530 "First element ($status_code) is an integer containing HTTP-like status code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001531 "(200 means OK, 4xx caller error, 5xx function error). Second element"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001532 "($reason) is a string containing error message, or something like \"OK\" if status is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001533 "200. Third element ($payload) is the actual result, but usually not present when enveloped result is an error response ($status_code is not 2xx). Fourth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001534 "element (%result_meta) is called result metadata and is optional, a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001535 "that contains extra information, much like how HTTP response headers provide additional metadata."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001536 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001537 "Return value:  (any)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001538 ""
